BrainBench world-v1 corpus (vendored)

Source:    https://github.com/garrytan/gbrain-evals
Commit:    b8cf8ad057635cbb03c0f3996acb693afbcae605
Path:      eval/data/world-v1/
Files:     241 *.json pages (~1.0 MB)
License:   MIT (see https://github.com/garrytan/gbrain-evals/blob/b8cf8ad/LICENSE)

This directory contains a verbatim copy of the world-v1 corpus
(`pages/*.json`) at the pinned commit above. Each page JSON carries
upstream's `slug`, `title`, `compiled_truth` (loaded as `body` via
serde alias in cairn-bench), `_facts`, `timeline`, and `type` fields
unchanged.

The derived snapshot files `queries.json` (145 graded queries) and
`upstream-baseline.json` (per-adapter per-query metrics) are produced
by running the upstream eval runner against the same pinned commit
and committed separately. See `scripts/README-brainbench-capture.md`
for the capture procedure (requires bun + OPENAI_API_KEY, ~$0.50 in
fees).

MIT License terms apply to the page JSONs. cairn's added derivations
(report renderer, adapter wiring) are licensed under cairn's own
license.
